# How I Work

## Docker

Everything runs in Docker. Never run npm install locally.

- Node deps: add to `package.json` (installed via Dockerfile)
- Python test deps: add to `requirements.txt` (installed via Dockerfile with pip)

To check if a change works:

```bash
docker compose down && docker compose up --build -d
```

Then wait for http://localhost:4444 to respond before testing.

## TDD

We first add the tests and security checks then we make the code to make them pass
First run the tests, run them and watch them fail due to missing functionality, then add the functionality. Tests in `tests/test_site.py`.
if you make changes, commit often and the tests will run on commit
so you're going to test some changes, just commit - keeps batches small and runs tests often

```bash
python -m unittest discover tests/
```

Tests run against the live Docker container using requests + BeautifulSoup.
Use `data-*` attributes on HTML elements to make them testable.

## Work in Small Batches

One piece flow.

## CI

GitHub Actions deploys to GitHub Pages on push to main.
Pre-push hook runs the full test suite -- if tests fail, the push is blocked.
